From: DevomB <Devom.hb@yahoo.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Read Kryptik's system config in place of the working directory's

havoc looks for havoc.cfg in the user's config directories, then in the
working directory. Kryptik ships its file under /usr, which every terminal,
zone 0's and a zone's, can read: that file is the last resort instead, and a
havoc.cfg in whatever directory a terminal starts in no longer configures it.
---
 main.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -1884,7 +1884,9 @@
 			return f;
 	}
 
-	f = fopen(CONF_FILE, "r");
+	/* Kryptik: the system's file, which a zone's terminal can read under /usr
+	 * too, rather than a havoc.cfg in the working directory. */
+	f = fopen("/usr/share/kryptik/havoc.cfg", "r");
 	return f;
 }
 
